@zeeg @tobi I think the intelligence levels between available models that people use will continue to increase

Very concretely, a behavior we see is that for less intelligent models you have to put a lot of hard constraints to avoid bad behaviors e.g. DO NOT WRITE COMMENTS but more intelligent models will use judgement well. But if you give the intelligent models the same constraints they will be forced to follow them.

I dont think this is going away.

@zeeg @tobi I think GPT and Claude models also have different behaviors in how to exercise judgement and the instructions that give the right amount of judgement to  them. 

As models get smarter you'll be asking them to do more ambitious things, which means there will still be an edge of their capability and judgement.

I realize this is maybe not worth to everyone to optimize, but I think there is a difference and will continue to exist.

